{"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","text":"Hypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edge position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":" is incidence number "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, and within a hyperedge in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)"},{"type":"text","text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a per-incidence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array must be rebuilt for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows: "},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shifted by n, and of "},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"Traversal","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ShortestPaths","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. "},{"code":"_withIncidentIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the view’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows out once per call from the base’s "},{"code":"_withIncidenceRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in O(n + m + p), for whole-graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range, O(1). On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its incidences, every read is O(1) plus"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the row. On any other base, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" binary-search the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedge and find the member by its rank ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)"},{"type":"text","text":"), O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" finds its place in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them on a base without a faster "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraphView, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"text":" gives the bipartite structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the view’s components restricted to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"text":" are the hypergraph’s.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0 ..< n + m","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"i < n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is hyperedge ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with an edge ","type":"text"},{"code":"{i, n + p}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it loses nothing.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/base","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edges-swift.property","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertices"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"gene